  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`NumberInput` is based on [react-number-format](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-number-format).\nIt supports most of the props from the `NumericFormat` component in the original package.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Value type",
      "text": "`value`, `defaultValue` and `onChange` props can be either string or number. In all cases\nwhen `NumberInput` value can be represented as a number, `onChange` function is called\nwith a number (for example `55`, `1.28`, `-100`, etc.). But there are several cases when\nit is not possible to represent value as a number:\n\n- Empty state is represented as an empty string – `''`\n- Numbers that are larger than `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` or smaller than `Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER` are represented as strings – `'90071992547409910'`\n- Numbers that consist of only multiple zeros are represented as strings – `0.`, `0.0`, `-0.00`, etc.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "min and max",
      "text": "Set `min` and `max` props to limit the input value:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Clamp behavior",
      "text": "By default, the value is clamped when the input is blurred. If you set `clampBehavior=\"strict\"`,\nit will not be possible to enter value outside of min/max range. Note that this option\nmay cause issues if you have tight `min` and `max`, for example `min={10}` and `max={20}`.\nIf you need to disable value clamping entirely, set `clampBehavior=\"none\"`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Prefix and suffix",
      "text": "Set `prefix` and `suffix` props to add given string to the start or end of the input value:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Negative numbers",
      "text": "By default, negative numbers are allowed. Set `allowNegative={false}` to allow only positive numbers.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Decimal numbers",
      "text": "By default, decimal numbers are allowed. Set `allowDecimal={false}` to allow only integers.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Decimal scale",
      "text": "`decimalScale` controls how many decimal places are allowed:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fixed decimal scale",
      "text": "Set `fixedDecimalScale` to always display fixed number of decimal places:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Decimal separator",
      "text": "Set `decimalSeparator` to change decimal separator character:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Thousand separator",
      "text": "Set `thousandSeparator` prop to separate thousands with a character. You can control\ngrouping logic with `thousandsGroupStyle`, it accepts: `thousand`, `lakh`, `wan`, `none` values.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Increment/decrement controls",
      "text": "By default, the right section is occupied by increment and decrement buttons.\nTo hide them, set `hideControls` prop. You can also use `rightSection` prop to render anything\nin the right section to replace the default controls.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Increment/decrement on hold",
      "text": "Set `stepHoldDelay` and `stepHoldInterval` props to define behavior when increment/decrement controls are clicked and hold:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Custom increment and decrement controls",
      "text": "You can get a ref with `increment` and `decrement` functions to create custom controls:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
